= Deliverables and grading

For this assignment there will be both a submitted file as well as an in-person presentation.

== Gradescope submission
For for deliverable you must submit to gradescope a PDF slideshow including
  + A title intro slide
  + A slide describing how you organized your collection
  + Your collection in Part 1 where there is a slide for each visualization including:
    + An image of the visualization
    + Description of what it is and how you found it
    + Source/link
  + Your critiques for Part 2 which for each chosen visualization must include a slide each detailing (briefly and in summary):
    + The annotated visualization showing and describing the different visual elements and how they are mapped to from data
    + A description of the context and goals of the visualization, what it is trying to say and to whom?
    + An analysis of what elements do a good or poor job in communicating the goal, and potentially what could be done differently.
  + A slide including your reflection on the assignment.


== Presentation
After you have submitted your presentation slides PDF, you will be able to actually present your findings to the rest of the class during scheduled lab time during Week 3. If you are not finished by the time of the scheduled presentations, or if you want to revise and resubmit your assignment you can re-present one-on-one during office hours or during extra time later during lab.

== Grade
You will be assessed based on:
  + Inclusion of all of the required components of the assignment.
  + Clear presentation detailing meaningful engagement with the chosen visualizations.
  + Your ability to respond to questions about the visualizations and your analysis beyond what is written directly on the slide.


